Negative control for collecting auth IN PLACE (D2 · the C4 ask).

Sends a guarded scenario to the standalone login page instead of its own
`<route>--auth` overlay, so the page the visitor asked for is left behind rather
than kept underneath — the "log in somewhere else and find your way back"
journey the ruling replaced.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the auth-collect spec — the rejection re-targets the page's own overlay,
whose name is the one the overlay registry injects.

